# A bar of 60 and one of 50 linked, the second set to move in a mechanism on its
# group screen and hinged to the first by a driven hinge, its turn the
# new parameter angle; the same as path_mechanism.go makes
# (TestPathEquivalence/mechanism). An empty model beside the parts is
# opened first, so that the links name them relative to it. The view is
# turned so that the upright edges, points seen from above, can be
# picked; both parts start where their files put them, and the second
# is the shorter, so that the first's far edge lies under none of it; it is hinged
# by its own far edge, as its first lies on the first part's.
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/host.tlspr
menu File|Open...
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/bar60.tlspr
menu Assembly|Link / Assemble...
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/bar50.tlspr
menu Assembly|Link / Assemble...
click-tw moves in a mechanism
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
click-entity 80030032
click-entity 80040032
menu Assembly|Mate Hinge, Driven
